      "content": "1. Definition of Verb"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Verbs are categorized primarily into Main Verbs and Auxiliary (Helping) Verbs.",
        "Auxiliary verbs are divided into Modal Auxiliary Verbs and Primary Auxiliary Verbs.",
        "Primary Auxiliary Verbs include forms of 'be', 'do', and 'have' which change according to person and tense.",
        "'Used to', 'Dare', and 'Need' serve distinct dual roles as main verbs and marginal modal auxiliaries.",
        "Understanding the various forms of verbs (V1, V2, V3, V4, V5) is essential for correct tense usage in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "8t33o98"
    },
